{
  "name": "Review & Reputation Engine",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⭐ REVIEW & REPUTATION ENGINE\n**What it does:** When a job completes → waits 2 days → emails the customer 5 clickable star links. Low ratings (1–3★) route to Slack support + sheet flips to `FLAGGED`; 4–5★ get your Google review link. A second flow checks your Google Business Profile reviews every morning, AI-summarizes sentiment, alerts Slack, and logs everything — ending in one Telegram digest.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- Gmail OAuth2 credential (the sending address)\n- Google Business Profile API access (Google Cloud Console → OAuth playground token; paste into CONFIG — GBP)\n- Slack API credential + a support channel name\n- OpenAI API key (platform.openai.com)\n- Google Sheets OAuth2 credential + one spreadsheet with tabs `Review Requests` and `GBP Reviews`\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID (@BotFather → /newbot)\n\n**Status flows:** `Review Requests` tab: `REQUEST_PENDING` → `REVIEW_ASKED` / `FLAGGED` · `GBP Reviews` tab: new → `LOGGED`",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 4200,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "d52a9f40-2e44-424e-ba1b-9db7d80f6970",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Job completed → 2-day wait → review request\nPOST /job-completed webhook (customer_name, email, phone, job_id) → CONFIG → log row as `REQUEST_PENDING` → respond OK → Wait 2 days → build 5 star-rating links → Gmail sends the review request email.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1900,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c1d88a2d-1edc-496d-b45d-178de0f7cc49",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — Rating webhook → smart routing\nCustomer clicks a star → GET /rate webhook (query: job_id, stars) → parse → match the job in Sheets → IF stars < 4: Slack alert to support + sheet → `FLAGGED`. Else: Gmail sends your Google review link + sheet → `REVIEW_ASKED`. Both branches merge → Flow-A summary.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 2200,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "905e14f2-6ec0-44fc-af53-0b17ac70f535",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1700,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — Daily Google Business Profile monitoring\n8 AM schedule → CONFIG — GBP (paste your OAuth token + account/location IDs) → list reviews via the GBP API → read already-seen review IDs from Sheets → keep only new ones → IF any new: AI Agent summarizes sentiment with a Structured Output Parser → Slack alert → append to `GBP Reviews` as `LOGGED`. No new reviews → quiet path.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 2400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b303ebf8-b97d-428c-9258-5e6d95347fe5",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        780
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Sheets logging + Telegram digest\nBoth flows feed one digest: new GBP reviews with sentiment counts, review requests sent, and flagged count — built by Build Daily Digest → CONFIG — Notifications → Telegram.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1600,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "adac82ac-a79f-400d-8c79-b799e01fa4fd",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2200,
        780
      ]
    },
